  <!--
    The toolbar and menu glyphs: Phosphor Icons 2.1.1 (MIT, see
    THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES-MAC.md), each one a single filled path on a 256-unit
    grid, which is what PathIcon draws. Generated from the package's SVGs;
    the key is what the app asks for, the comment is the Phosphor name, so
    a glyph can be swapped by looking it up there.

    Monochrome on purpose. A Mac toolbar is drawn in the label colour and
    tinted by the system, and the painted artwork belongs on the tiles,
    where it has room to be seen.
  -->
